    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **274 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented digits-only telephone storage with normalization applied before the uniqueness check.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted numbers like `(613) 555-0100` pass the `@Valid` bean-validation on the request DTO (previously they'd be rejected with a 400 before ever reaching the controller). Also updated the field description.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeTelephone(...)` helper that strips all non-digit characters (spaces, dashes, parentheses), and applied it:\n   - In `addOwner`, right after mapping the DTO to the entity \u2014 so normalization happens **before** the `isDuplicateOwner` uniqueness check and before persistence. This makes `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide as duplicates and both store as `6135550100`.\n   - In `updateOwner`, when setting the telephone, for consistent digits-only storage.\n\nThe stored (normalized) value is what gets returned in the `telephone` field, since the response is mapped from the persisted entity. The `Owner` entity's existing `^[0-9]{10}$` constraint continues to hold because the stored value is now always digits.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`Cp11Tests.coreStoresDigitsOnly` and `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
